\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The two pairings in the volume factor}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{In the [reference-volume Jacobian](fdip-00JI),
#{T^\dagger T} acts on the source space even when the two carriers are
different. Its determinant therefore belongs to a single endomorphism.
The [chosen-pairing adjoint](fdip-001P) uses the two counting inner
products; no quadratic precision enters this definition.}
